Bounded private helper substitution — 2026-10-16

New optional leaves may contain fixed scalar or pointer locals. They must
retain the existing 48-node leaf limit and have no calls, loops, escaped
objects, activation-sensitive operations, assembly or statement expressions.
The new class excludes attributed functions/locals, static storage, cleanup,
volatile/atomic locals and VM capture objects. Existing explicit-inline paths
are unchanged. A unit has 1024 source-node cost units for these new calls,
including calls inside another expansion. This is not a machine-byte bound.
When the budget runs out, the call remains. The rewritten reference closure
keeps its callable definition. No independent checker is changed.

